@lang en
IMPORT `pru-benefits`

-- Tests of the Rules and Terms. Every expected value was worked out by hand from the source
-- text (the percentages, caps, periods and dates it prints) before the assertion was run; the
-- arithmetic is in the comment beside each group. Scenario values (a sum insured of 1 billion
-- VND, premiums of 30 million) are the tester's, from pru-fixtures.l4. A failing assertion
-- here is a finding, never a value to edit.
-- The ordinary case: `the policy` (1,000,000,000 VND, 10 years from 2026-01-15, insured born
-- 1990-06-01, so the term ends 2036-01-15); `the accident` (2027-03-10, no excluded cause).

§ `Tests of the Rules and Terms`

§§ `Part I — eligibility, age, dates, in force`

-- 1.2, 1.3, 2.2: an adult insuring themself for 10 years is eligible.
#ASSERT `Part I — the application meets the eligibility terms` (`an application by` (`an adult resident born` (YMD 1990 6 1)) `for` `the insured is the policyholder` `born` (YMD 1990 6 1) `entering on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `for a term of` 10)
-- 1.2: a policyholder aged 17 at entry may not be one; aged 18 may.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 1.2 — may be the policyholder` (`an adult resident born` (YMD 2008 6 1)) (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT `Article 1.2 — may be the policyholder` (`an adult resident born` (YMD 2008 1 15)) (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 1.2 — an insurable interest` `none of these`
-- 1.3: "từ 6 tháng": 6 months old on the day of entry is enough, one day short is not.
#ASSERT `Article 1.3 — the insured is eligible` (`an application by` `a company` `for` `another person in whom the policyholder has an insurable interest` `born` (YMD 2025 7 15) `entering on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `for a term of` 10)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 1.3 — the insured is eligible` (`an application by` `a company` `for` `another person in whom the policyholder has an insurable interest` `born` (YMD 2025 7 16) `entering on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `for a term of` 10)
-- 1.3: 65 at entry with a 5-year term ends at 70: eligible; with 10 years, 75: not; 66: not.
#ASSERT `Article 1.3 — the insured is eligible` (`an application by` `a company` `for` `another person in whom the policyholder has an insurable interest` `born` (YMD 1960 6 1) `entering on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `for a term of` 5)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 1.3 — the insured is eligible` (`an application by` `a company` `for` `another person in whom the policyholder has an insurable interest` `born` (YMD 1960 6 1) `entering on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `for a term of` 10)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 1.3 — the insured is eligible` (`an application by` `a company` `for` `another person in whom the policyholder has an insurable interest` `born` (YMD 1960 1 1) `entering on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `for a term of` 5)
-- 2.2: 5, 10, 15 and nothing else.
#ASSERT `Article 2.2 — a term the policyholder may choose` 15
#ASSERT NOT `Article 2.2 — a term the policyholder may choose` 7

-- 1.4: age last birthday.
#ASSERT `age last birthday of someone born` (YMD 1990 6 1) `on the date` (YMD 2027 5 31) EQUALS 36
#ASSERT `age last birthday of someone born` (YMD 1990 6 1) `on the date` (YMD 2027 6 1) EQUALS 37
-- 1.8: contract year 1 runs to the day before the first anniversary.
#ASSERT `the contract year of` `the policy` `in which falls` (YMD 2027 1 14) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the contract year of` `the policy` `in which falls` (YMD 2027 1 15) EQUALS 2
-- 1.10 and 2.2: 10 years from 2026-01-15; for an insured born 1961-06-01 the 70th birthday
-- (2031-06-01) cuts it at the next anniversary, 2032-01-15.
#ASSERT `the end of the contract term of` `the policy` EQUALS YMD 2036 1 15
#ASSERT `the end of the contract term of` (`the same policy for` 1_000_000_000 `on an insured born` (YMD 1961 6 1)) EQUALS YMD 2032 1 15
#ASSERT NOT `the term runs its chosen length` (`the same policy for` 1_000_000_000 `on an insured born` (YMD 1961 6 1))
-- In force: from the effective date to the end of the term; not during a lapse.
#ASSERT `the policy` `in force on` (YMD 2026 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `the policy` `in force on` (YMD 2026 1 14)
#ASSERT `the policy` `in force on` (YMD 2036 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `the policy` `in force on` (YMD 2036 1 16)
#ASSERT NOT (`the policy, lapsed on` (YMD 2027 1 1) `and reinstated on` (JUST (YMD 2027 6 1))) `in force on` (YMD 2027 3 10)
#ASSERT (`the policy, lapsed on` (YMD 2027 1 1) `and reinstated on` (JUST (YMD 2027 6 1))) `in force on` (YMD 2027 6 1)
#ASSERT (`the policy, lapsed on` (YMD 2027 1 1) `and reinstated on` (JUST (YMD 2027 6 1))) `in force on` (YMD 2026 12 31)
-- 1.13: a surrender value from the second anniversary, once 24 months of premium are paid.
#ASSERT `Article 1.13 — the contract has a surrender value` `the policy` TRUE `on` (YMD 2028 1 15)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 1.13 — the contract has a surrender value` `the policy` TRUE `on` (YMD 2028 1 14)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 1.13 — the contract has a surrender value` `the policy` FALSE `on` (YMD 2030 1 15)

§§ `Part I — definitions that decide cover`

-- 1.16: all four limbs; an event that was not the sole cause is not an Accident.
#ASSERT `Article 1.16 — an Accident` `the accident`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 1.16 — an Accident` (`an event that was not the sole cause, on` (YMD 2027 3 10))
-- 1.17: paralysis certified no sooner than 6 months after onset (2027-03-10 -> 2027-09-10).
#ASSERT NOT `Article 1.17 — total and permanent disability` (`a disability of` (JUST `both legs`) `by paralysis` TRUE `capacity lost` NOTHING `from` (YMD 2027 3 10) `certified` (YMD 2027 9 9))
#ASSERT `Article 1.17 — total and permanent disability` (`a disability of` (JUST `both legs`) `by paralysis` TRUE `capacity lost` NOTHING `from` (YMD 2027 3 10) `certified` (YMD 2027 9 10))
-- A lost body part may be certified at once.
#ASSERT `Article 1.17 — total and permanent disability` (`a disability of` (JUST `one hand and one leg`) `by paralysis` FALSE `capacity lost` NOTHING `from` (YMD 2027 3 10) `certified` (YMD 2027 3 11))
-- 1.17(b): 81% loss of working capacity, not 80%.
#ASSERT `Article 1.17 — total and permanent disability` (`a disability of` NOTHING `by paralysis` FALSE `capacity lost` (JUST 81) `from` (YMD 2027 3 10) `certified` (YMD 2027 9 10))
#ASSERT NOT `Article 1.17 — total and permanent disability` (`a disability of` NOTHING `by paralysis` FALSE `capacity lost` (JUST 80) `from` (YMD 2027 3 10) `certified` (YMD 2027 9 10))
-- 1.19: a coma of 96 hours, not 95; the skull-fracture limb, not a linear vault fracture alone.
#ASSERT `Article 1.19 — a brain injury` (`a coma in hours of` 96)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 1.19 — a brain injury` (`a coma in hours of` 95)
#ASSERT `Article 1.19 — a brain injury` (`a depressed skull fracture with surgery, linear vault fracture only` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 1.19 — a brain injury` (`a depressed skull fracture with surgery, linear vault fracture only` TRUE)
-- 1.20: a greenstick break is no Fracture; nor one confirmed only by the insured's brother (1.25).
#ASSERT `Article 1.20 — a Fracture` (`a fracture of` `a rib` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `previously broken` NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 1.20 — a Fracture` (`a greenstick fracture of` `a rib` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10))
#ASSERT NOT `Article 1.20 — a Fracture` (`a fracture of` `a rib` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `confirmed only by the insured's brother`)
-- 1.23, 1.24.
#ASSERT `Article 1.23 — a Hospital` (`a facility of kind` `a hospital`)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 1.23 — a Hospital` (`a facility of kind` `a general clinic`)
#ASSERT `Article 1.24 — an intensive care unit` (`an intensive care unit in` (`a facility of kind` `a hospital`) `which is an emergency room` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 1.24 — an intensive care unit` (`an intensive care unit in` (`a facility of kind` `a hospital`) `which is an emergency room` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 1.24 — an intensive care unit` (`an intensive care unit in` (`a facility of kind` `a general clinic`) `which is an emergency room` FALSE)

§§ `Article 3 — temporary cover`

-- Application and first premium 2026-01-02, certificate issued 2026-01-15.
-- Benefit: the lesser of 200,000,000 and the sum insured applied for.
#ASSERT `Article 3 — what is paid on a death during temporary cover` (`The temporary cover` OF (YMD 2026 1 2), JUST (YMD 2026 1 15), 1_000_000_000) (`a death on` (YMD 2026 1 10) `from` (JUST (`an accident on` (YMD 2026 1 9) `with` `no excluded cause`)) `as` `any other circumstance`) `the accounts` EQUALS `the temporary cover benefit` 200_000_000
#ASSERT `Article 3 — what is paid on a death during temporary cover` (`The temporary cover` OF (YMD 2026 1 2), JUST (YMD 2026 1 15), 150_000_000) (`a death on` (YMD 2026 1 10) `from` (JUST (`an accident on` (YMD 2026 1 9) `with` `no excluded cause`)) `as` `any other circumstance`) `the accounts` EQUALS `the temporary cover benefit` 150_000_000
-- Premiums above 200,000,000: refunded instead.
#ASSERT `Article 3 — what is paid on a death during temporary cover` (`The temporary cover` OF (YMD 2026 1 2), JUST (YMD 2026 1 15), 1_000_000_000) (`a death on` (YMD 2026 1 10) `from` (JUST (`an accident on` (YMD 2026 1 9) `with` `no excluded cause`)) `as` `any other circumstance`) (`accounts with premiums` 250_000_000 `surrender value` NOTHING `debts` NOTHING `medical costs` NOTHING) EQUALS `the premiums paid, refunded instead of the temporary cover benefit` 250_000_000
-- An excluded cause, direct or indirect: the premium less the medical costs (30m - 5m).
#ASSERT `Article 3 — what is paid on a death during temporary cover` (`The temporary cover` OF (YMD 2026 1 2), JUST (YMD 2026 1 15), 1_000_000_000) (`a death on` (YMD 2026 1 10) `from` (JUST (`an accident on` (YMD 2026 1 9) `with` (`a dangerous activity, linked as` `indirectly caused by it`))) `as` `any other circumstance`) (`accounts with premiums` 30_000_000 `surrender value` NOTHING `debts` NOTHING `medical costs` (JUST 5_000_000)) EQUALS `the premiums paid, refunded less medical examination costs, for an excluded death` 25_000_000
-- After the certificate is issued, Article 3 no longer applies.
#ASSERT `Article 3 — what is paid on a death during temporary cover` (`The temporary cover` OF (YMD 2026 1 2), JUST (YMD 2026 1 15), 1_000_000_000) (`a death on` (YMD 2026 1 16) `from` (JUST (`an accident on` (YMD 2026 1 9) `with` `no excluded cause`)) `as` `any other circumstance`) `the accounts` EQUALS `nothing under Article 3: the death was outside the temporary cover period`
-- A death not caused by an Accident: Article 3 is silent (finding F-09).
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 3 — what is paid on a death during temporary cover` (`The temporary cover` OF (YMD 2026 1 2), NOTHING, 1_000_000_000) (`a death on` (YMD 2026 1 10) `from` NOTHING `as` `any other circumstance`) `the accounts` BECAUSE "Article 3 does not say what is paid when the insured dies during temporary cover other than by an Accident"

§§ `Article 4 — the free-look period`

-- Certificate received 2026-01-20; 21 days run to 2026-02-10.
#ASSERT `Article 4 — the notice refusing the contract is in time` (YMD 2026 1 20) (YMD 2026 2 10)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 4 — the notice refusing the contract is in time` (YMD 2026 1 20) (YMD 2026 2 11)
#ASSERT `Article 4 — the refund on a refusal` (`accounts with premiums` 30_000_000 `surrender value` NOTHING `debts` NOTHING `medical costs` (JUST 2_000_000)) EQUALS 28_000_000
#TRACE `Article 4 — the free look` `the accounts` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the policyholder` DOES `give written notice refusing to continue the contract` AT 21
    PARTY `Prudential` DOES `refund the premiums paid, less medical examination costs` AT 40

§§ `Article 5 — a misstated age or sex`

-- Not acceptable at the true age: the greater of premiums (30m) and surrender value (40m),
-- less benefits paid (5m), medical costs (1m) and debts (2m) = 32m.
#ASSERT `Article 5 — the adjustment` (`A misstated age or sex` OF 1_000_000, 1_200_000, 0, 833_000_000, FALSE, 5_000_000) (`accounts with premiums` 30_000_000 `surrender value` (JUST 40_000_000) `debts` (JUST 2_000_000) `medical costs` (JUST 1_000_000)) EQUALS `the contract is cancelled and Prudential pays` 32_000_000
#ASSERT `Article 5 — the adjustment` (`A misstated age or sex` OF 1_000_000, 1_200_000, 0, 833_000_000, TRUE, 0) `the accounts` EQUALS `the sum insured is adjusted to` 833_000_000
#ASSERT `Article 5 — the adjustment` (`A misstated age or sex` OF 1_200_000, 1_000_000, 3_000_000, 1_200_000_000, TRUE, 0) `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential refunds the excess premium` 3_000_000
#ASSERT `Article 5 — the adjustment` (`A misstated age or sex` OF 1_000_000, 1_000_000, 0, 1_000_000_000, TRUE, 0) `the accounts` EQUALS `no adjustment is needed`

§§ `Article 6 — incontestability`

-- 24 months from 2026-01-15 is 2028-01-15. A material misstatement may be raised at any time.
#ASSERT `Article 6 — Prudential may still raise the misstatement` `the policy` (`A misstatement` OF TRUE, YMD 2035 1 1)
#ASSERT `Article 6 — Prudential may still raise the misstatement` `the policy` (`A misstatement` OF FALSE, YMD 2028 1 14)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 6 — Prudential may still raise the misstatement` `the policy` (`A misstatement` OF FALSE, YMD 2028 1 15)
-- After a reinstatement on 2027-06-01 the 24 months run from it, to 2029-06-01.
#ASSERT `Article 6 — Prudential may still raise the misstatement` (`the policy, lapsed on` (YMD 2027 1 1) `and reinstated on` (JUST (YMD 2027 6 1))) (`A misstatement` OF FALSE, YMD 2029 5 31)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 6 — Prudential may still raise the misstatement` (`the policy, lapsed on` (YMD 2027 1 1) `and reinstated on` (JUST (YMD 2027 6 1))) (`A misstatement` OF FALSE, YMD 2029 6 1)

§§ `Article 7 — succession`

#ASSERT `Article 7 — what happens` (`an application by` (`an adult resident born` (YMD 1985 1 1)) `for` `a lawful spouse, child or parent of the policyholder, natural or adoptive` `born` (YMD 1990 6 1) `entering on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `for a term of` 10) (`A change in the policyholder` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) `the accounts` EQUALS `the lawful heir inherits the policyholder's rights and obligations`
-- The heir does not qualify: the greater of 30m and 50m, less 1m and 4m = 45m.
#ASSERT `Article 7 — what happens` (`an application by` (`an adult resident born` (YMD 1985 1 1)) `for` `a lawful spouse, child or parent of the policyholder, natural or adoptive` `born` (YMD 1990 6 1) `entering on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `for a term of` 10) (`A change in the policyholder` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) (`accounts with premiums` 30_000_000 `surrender value` (JUST 50_000_000) `debts` (JUST 4_000_000) `medical costs` (JUST 1_000_000)) EQUALS `the contract terminates early and Prudential pays` 45_000_000
#ASSERT `Article 7 — what happens` (`an application by` `a company` `for` `another person in whom the policyholder has an insurable interest` `born` (YMD 1990 6 1) `entering on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `for a term of` 10) (`A change in the policyholder` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE) `the accounts` EQUALS `the insured becomes the new policyholder; the original policyholder's beneficiaries are cancelled`
#ASSERT `Article 7 — what happens` (`an application by` `a company` `for` `another person in whom the policyholder has an insurable interest` `born` (YMD 1990 6 1) `entering on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `for a term of` 10) (`A change in the policyholder` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE) `the accounts` EQUALS `Article 7 does not apply`
#ASSERT `Article 7 — what happens` (`an application by` (`an adult resident born` (YMD 1990 6 1)) `for` `the insured is the policyholder` `born` (YMD 1990 6 1) `entering on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `for a term of` 10) (`A change in the policyholder` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) `the accounts` EQUALS `Article 7 does not apply`

§§ `Article 8.1, 8.7, 11.2 — death`

-- 8.1(a)-(c): 100%, 200% (scheduled public land transport), 300% (scheduled flight).
#ASSERT `the death claim` `the policy` (`a death on` (YMD 2027 3 20) `from` (JUST `the accident`) `as` `any other circumstance`) `the accounts` `nothing paid yet` EQUALS `the accidental death benefit, Article 8.1` 1_000_000_000
#ASSERT `the death claim` `the policy` (`a death on` (YMD 2027 3 20) `from` (JUST `the accident`) `as` `a ticketed passenger on licensed public commercial land transport on a regular schedule and an established route`) `the accounts` `nothing paid yet` EQUALS `the accidental death benefit, Article 8.1` 2_000_000_000
#ASSERT `the death claim` `the policy` (`a death on` (YMD 2027 3 20) `from` (JUST `the accident`) `as` `a ticketed passenger on a licensed commercial flight on a regular schedule and an established route`) `the accounts` `nothing paid yet` EQUALS `the accidental death benefit, Article 8.1` 3_000_000_000
-- The 180 days: day 180 pays; day 181 is the gap of finding F-01.
#ASSERT `the death claim` `the policy` (`a death on` ((YMD 2027 3 10) PLUS 180) `from` (JUST `the accident`) `as` `any other circumstance`) `the accounts` `nothing paid yet` EQUALS `the accidental death benefit, Article 8.1` 1_000_000_000
#ASSERT `the death claim` `the policy` (`a death on` ((YMD 2027 3 10) PLUS 181) `from` (JUST `the accident`) `as` `any other circumstance`) `the accounts` `nothing paid yet` EQUALS `no Article of the Rules and Terms pays for this death`
-- 8.10: injury benefits (200m) paid for the accident come off a death within 30 days, not 31.
#ASSERT `the death claim` `the policy` (`a death on` ((YMD 2027 3 10) PLUS 30) `from` (JUST `the accident`) `as` `any other circumstance`) `the accounts` (`already paid: permanent injury` 200_000_000 `organ` 0 `fracture` 0 `burn` 0 `ambulance this year` 0 `injury benefits for this accident` 200_000_000) EQUALS `the accidental death benefit, Article 8.1` 800_000_000
#ASSERT `the death claim` `the policy` (`a death on` ((YMD 2027 3 10) PLUS 31) `from` (JUST `the accident`) `as` `any other circumstance`) `the accounts` (`already paid: permanent injury` 200_000_000 `organ` 0 `fracture` 0 `burn` 0 `ambulance this year` 0 `injury benefits for this accident` 200_000_000) EQUALS `the accidental death benefit, Article 8.1` 1_000_000_000
-- 8.10: debts of 5m come off.
#ASSERT `the death claim` `the policy` (`a death on` (YMD 2027 3 20) `from` (JUST `the accident`) `as` `any other circumstance`) (`accounts with premiums` 30_000_000 `surrender value` NOTHING `debts` (JUST 5_000_000) `medical costs` NOTHING) `nothing paid yet` EQUALS `the accidental death benefit, Article 8.1` 995_000_000
-- 8.7: a death not caused by an Accident, or by an event that fails 1.16: the premiums, 30m.
#ASSERT `the death claim` `the policy` (`a death on` (YMD 2027 3 20) `from` NOTHING `as` `any other circumstance`) `the accounts` `nothing paid yet` EQUALS `the non-accidental death benefit, Article 8.7` 30_000_000
#ASSERT `the death claim` `the policy` (`a death on` (YMD 2027 3 20) `from` (JUST (`an event that was not the sole cause, on` (YMD 2027 3 10))) `as` `any other circumstance`) `the accounts` `nothing paid yet` EQUALS `the non-accidental death benefit, Article 8.7` 30_000_000
-- 11.1(a) and 11.2: war as the direct cause: the greater of premiums and surrender value, less debts.
#ASSERT `the death claim` `the policy` (`a death on` (YMD 2027 3 20) `from` (JUST (`an accident on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `with` (`war, linked as` `directly caused by it`))) `as` `any other circumstance`) `the accounts` `nothing paid yet` EQUALS `the excluded-death payment, Article 11.2` 30_000_000
#ASSERT `the death claim` `the policy` (`a death on` (YMD 2027 3 20) `from` (JUST (`an accident on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `with` (`war, linked as` `directly caused by it`))) `as` `any other circumstance`) (`accounts with premiums` 30_000_000 `surrender value` (JUST 40_000_000) `debts` (JUST 5_000_000) `medical costs` NOTHING) `nothing paid yet` EQUALS `the excluded-death payment, Article 11.2` 35_000_000
-- Near miss: war only an indirect cause is not excluded by 11.1.
#ASSERT `the death claim` `the policy` (`a death on` (YMD 2027 3 20) `from` (JUST (`an accident on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `with` (`war, linked as` `indirectly caused by it`))) `as` `any other circumstance`) `the accounts` `nothing paid yet` EQUALS `the accidental death benefit, Article 8.1` 1_000_000_000
-- After the end of the term (2036-01-15) nothing is paid.
#ASSERT `the death claim` `the policy` (`a death on` (YMD 2036 1 20) `from` (JUST (`an accident on` (YMD 2036 1 10) `with` `no excluded cause`)) `as` `any other circumstance`) `the accounts` `nothing paid yet` EQUALS `nothing, because the contract was not in force at the death`

§§ `Article 11.1 — each exclusion, triggered and near missed`

-- Through the fracture benefit, whose claim names every head that can reach it.
#ASSERT `Article 11.1 — the exclusions that apply` `the policy` (`an accident on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `with` (`war, linked as` `directly caused by it`)) `the fracture benefit (8.4)` (YMD 2027 3 10) EQUALS LIST `(a) war, belligerent acts, rebellion, civil disorder or riot`
#ASSERT null (`Article 11.1 — the exclusions that apply` `the policy` (`an accident on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `with` (`war, linked as` `related to it, but not caused by it`)) `the fracture benefit (8.4)` (YMD 2027 3 10))
#ASSERT `Article 11.1 — the exclusions that apply` `the policy` (`an accident on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `with` (`a crime, linked as` `directly caused by it` `concluded by an authority` TRUE)) `the fracture benefit (8.4)` (YMD 2027 3 10) EQUALS LIST `(b) a crime, as a competent State authority concluded`
#ASSERT null (`Article 11.1 — the exclusions that apply` `the policy` (`an accident on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `with` (`a crime, linked as` `directly caused by it` `concluded by an authority` FALSE)) `the fracture benefit (8.4)` (YMD 2027 3 10))
#ASSERT `Article 11.1 — the exclusions that apply` `the policy` (`an accident on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `with` (`suicide or self-injury, linked as` `directly caused by it`)) `the fracture benefit (8.4)` (YMD 2027 3 10) EQUALS LIST `(c) suicide or self-inflicted injury`
#ASSERT null (`Article 11.1 — the exclusions that apply` `the policy` (`an accident on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `with` (`suicide or self-injury, linked as` `indirectly caused by it`)) `the fracture benefit (8.4)` (YMD 2027 3 10))
#ASSERT `Article 11.1 — the exclusions that apply` `the policy` (`an accident on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `with` (`a dangerous activity, linked as` `directly caused by it`)) `the fracture benefit (8.4)` (YMD 2027 3 10) EQUALS LIST `(d) a dangerous activity`
#ASSERT null (`Article 11.1 — the exclusions that apply` `the policy` (`an accident on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `with` (`a dangerous activity, linked as` `not related to it`)) `the fracture benefit (8.4)` (YMD 2027 3 10))
#ASSERT `Article 11.1 — the exclusions that apply` `the policy` (`an accident on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `with` (`a substance, linked as` `directly caused by it` `prescribed` FALSE `and the cause of the Accident` TRUE)) `the fracture benefit (8.4)` (YMD 2027 3 10) EQUALS LIST `(e) the influence of a substance`
#ASSERT null (`Article 11.1 — the exclusions that apply` `the policy` (`an accident on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `with` (`a substance, linked as` `directly caused by it` `prescribed` TRUE `and the cause of the Accident` TRUE)) `the fracture benefit (8.4)` (YMD 2027 3 10))
#ASSERT `Article 11.1 — the exclusions that apply` `the policy` (`an accident on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `with` (`an intentional act, linked as` `directly caused by it` `by one of several beneficiaries` FALSE)) `the fracture benefit (8.4)` (YMD 2027 3 10) EQUALS LIST `(f) an intentional act`
#ASSERT null (`Article 11.1 — the exclusions that apply` `the policy` (`an accident on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `with` (`an intentional act, linked as` `directly caused by it` `by one of several beneficiaries` TRUE)) `the fracture benefit (8.4)` (YMD 2027 3 10))
-- (g): an accident the day before the effective date, and one on it.
#ASSERT `Article 11.1 — the exclusions that apply` `the policy` (`an accident on` (YMD 2026 1 14) `with` `no excluded cause`) `the fracture benefit (8.4)` (YMD 2026 1 14) EQUALS LIST `(g) an accident or condition before the effective or reinstatement date`
#ASSERT null (`Article 11.1 — the exclusions that apply` `the policy` (`an accident on` (YMD 2026 1 15) `with` `no excluded cause`) `the fracture benefit (8.4)` (YMD 2026 1 15))
-- (h): reaches a fracture, not a burn.
#ASSERT `Article 11.1 — the exclusions that apply` `the policy` (`an accident on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `with` (`an illness or treatment, linked as` `directly caused by it`)) `the fracture benefit (8.4)` (YMD 2027 3 10) EQUALS LIST `(h) a consequence of illness or of treatment`
#ASSERT null (`Article 11.1 — the exclusions that apply` `the policy` (`an accident on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `with` (`an illness or treatment, linked as` `directly caused by it`)) `the burn benefit (8.5)` (YMD 2027 3 10))
-- 11.3: 1bn to beneficiaries of 50, 30 and 20; the third harmed the insured: 625m and 375m.
#ASSERT `Article 11.3 — the shares paid` 1_000_000_000 (LIST `beneficiary` "A" `share` 50 `alive` TRUE `harmed the insured` FALSE, `beneficiary` "B" `share` 30 `alive` TRUE `harmed the insured` FALSE, `beneficiary` "C" `share` 20 `alive` TRUE `harmed the insured` TRUE) EQUALS LIST 625_000_000, 375_000_000

§§ `Article 8.2 — permanent injury`

-- One hand: 50% of 1bn.
#ASSERT `Article 8.2 — the permanent-injury benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (LIST `loss of one hand`) (YMD 2027 3 10) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 500_000_000
-- Both hands and one eye, one accident: 100% + 50%, capped at 100%.
#ASSERT `Article 8.2 — the permanent-injury benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (LIST `loss of both hands`, `loss of one eye`) (YMD 2027 3 10) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 1_000_000_000
-- 800m already paid in the term: one leg (500m) is cut to the 200m left.
#ASSERT `Article 8.2 — the permanent-injury benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (LIST `loss of one leg`) (YMD 2027 3 10) (`already paid: permanent injury` 800_000_000 `organ` 0 `fracture` 0 `burn` 0 `ambulance this year` 0 `injury benefits for this accident` 0) `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 200_000_000
#ASSERT `Article 8.2 — the permanent-injury benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (LIST `loss of one leg`) (YMD 2027 3 10) (`already paid: permanent injury` 1_000_000_000 `organ` 0 `fracture` 0 `burn` 0 `ambulance this year` 0 `injury benefits for this accident` 0) `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays nothing, because` `the maximum for the contract term has already been paid`
-- Brain injury: a coma of 96 hours qualifies (100%); 95 does not.
#ASSERT `Article 8.2 — the permanent-injury benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (LIST `brain injury` (`a coma in hours of` 96)) (YMD 2027 3 10) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 1_000_000_000
#ASSERT `Article 8.2 — the permanent-injury benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (LIST `brain injury` (`a coma in hours of` 95)) (YMD 2027 3 10) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays nothing, because` `the injury is not one the payout-rate table lists`
-- 11.1(g): the accident the day before the effective date, the amputation after it.
#ASSERT `Article 8.2 — the permanent-injury benefit` `the policy` (`an accident on` (YMD 2026 1 14) `with` `no excluded cause`) (LIST `loss of one hand`) (YMD 2026 2 1) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays nothing, because` `excluded by Article 11.1`
-- 8.2 and 16: paid to the maximum, the contract ends.
#ASSERT `Article 8.2 — the contract ends with this payment` `the policy` 400_000_000 (`already paid: permanent injury` 600_000_000 `organ` 0 `fracture` 0 `burn` 0 `ambulance this year` 0 `injury benefits for this accident` 0)
#ASSERT NOT `Article 8.2 — the contract ends with this payment` `the policy` 300_000_000 (`already paid: permanent injury` 600_000_000 `organ` 0 `fracture` 0 `burn` 0 `ambulance this year` 0 `injury benefits for this accident` 0)

§§ `Article 8.3 — internal organ injury`

-- Spleen and liver: 5% + 5% of 1bn.
#ASSERT `Article 8.3 — the internal-organ benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (LIST `ruptured spleen`, `ruptured liver`) (YMD 2027 3 10) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 100_000_000
#ASSERT `Article 8.3 — the internal-organ benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (LIST `an organ injury the table does not list` "bruised lung") (YMD 2027 3 10) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays nothing, because` `the injury is not one the payout-rate table lists`

§§ `Article 8.4 — fracture`

-- Adult (36): femur and tibia are one "one or more" row (30%, once), two ribs 10% each:
-- 50% of 1bn = 500m, within the cap of the lesser of 1bn and 500m.
#ASSERT `Article 8.4 — the fracture benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (LIST `a fracture of` `one or more leg bones: femur, patella, tibia, fibula` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `previously broken` NOTHING, `a fracture of` `one or more leg bones: femur, patella, tibia, fibula` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `previously broken` NOTHING, `a fracture of` `a rib` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `previously broken` NOTHING, `a fracture of` `a rib` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `previously broken` NOTHING) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 500_000_000
-- Adult spine: 100% = 1bn, cut to the adult cap of 500m.
#ASSERT `Article 8.4 — the fracture benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (LIST `a fracture of` `the spine, except the coccyx` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `previously broken` NOTHING) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 500_000_000
-- The age bands, on the age last birthday at the accident (2027-03-10):
-- born 2021-03-11, aged 5: 50% of 1bn = 500m; born 2021-03-10, aged 6: the lesser of 1bn and 250m.
#ASSERT `Article 8.4 — the fracture benefit` (`the same policy for` 1_000_000_000 `on an insured born` (YMD 2021 3 11)) `the accident` (LIST `a fracture of` `the spine, except the coccyx` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `previously broken` NOTHING) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 500_000_000
#ASSERT `Article 8.4 — the fracture benefit` (`the same policy for` 1_000_000_000 `on an insured born` (YMD 2021 3 10)) `the accident` (LIST `a fracture of` `the spine, except the coccyx` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `previously broken` NOTHING) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 250_000_000
-- born 2009-03-11, aged 17: 250m; born 2009-03-10, aged 18: 500m.
#ASSERT `Article 8.4 — the fracture benefit` (`the same policy for` 1_000_000_000 `on an insured born` (YMD 2009 3 11)) `the accident` (LIST `a fracture of` `the spine, except the coccyx` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `previously broken` NOTHING) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 250_000_000
#ASSERT `Article 8.4 — the fracture benefit` (`the same policy for` 1_000_000_000 `on an insured born` (YMD 2009 3 10)) `the accident` (LIST `a fracture of` `the spine, except the coccyx` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `previously broken` NOTHING) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 500_000_000
-- The 10-month rule: previous fracture 2026-05-10 (10 months exactly) pays; 2026-05-11 does not.
#ASSERT `Article 8.4 — the fracture benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (LIST `a fracture of` `a rib` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `previously broken` (JUST (YMD 2026 5 10))) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 100_000_000
#ASSERT `Article 8.4 — the fracture benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (LIST `a fracture of` `a rib` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `previously broken` (JUST (YMD 2026 5 11))) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays nothing, because` `the same bone broke less than 10 months after its previous fracture`
-- 1.20: a greenstick break pays nothing.
#ASSERT `Article 8.4 — the fracture benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (LIST `a greenstick fracture of` `a rib` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10)) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays nothing, because` `the break is not a Fracture as Article 1.20 defines it`
-- The cap counts earlier payments: 450m paid, a wrist (15% = 150m) gets the 50m left.
#ASSERT `Article 8.4 — the fracture benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (LIST `a fracture of` `a wrist bone` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `previously broken` NOTHING) (`already paid: permanent injury` 0 `organ` 0 `fracture` 450_000_000 `burn` 0 `ambulance this year` 0 `injury benefits for this accident` 0) `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 50_000_000
-- 11.1(h): a fracture from osteoporosis.
#ASSERT `Article 8.4 — the fracture benefit` `the policy` (`an accident on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `with` (`an illness or treatment, linked as` `directly caused by it`)) (LIST `a fracture of` `a rib` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `previously broken` NOTHING) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays nothing, because` `excluded by Article 11.1`

§§ `Article 8.5 — burns`

-- Adult: 25% third degree is the 100% row, 1bn, cut to the 500m cap.
#ASSERT `Article 8.5 — the burn benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (`a burn of` 25 `percent at third degree and` 0 `percent at second degree`) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 500_000_000
-- Sum insured 400m: 20% second degree is the 50% row, 200m, within the cap of 400m.
#ASSERT `Article 8.5 — the burn benefit` (`the same policy for` 400_000_000 `on an insured born` (YMD 1990 6 1)) `the accident` (`a burn of` 0 `percent at third degree and` 20 `percent at second degree`) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 200_000_000
-- 8% at third degree is in no row.
#ASSERT `Article 8.5 — the burn benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (`a burn of` 8 `percent at third degree and` 0 `percent at second degree`) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays nothing, because` `the injury is not one the payout-rate table lists`
-- 11.1(h) does not reach burns: a burn from treatment is paid (25% row, 250m).
#ASSERT `Article 8.5 — the burn benefit` `the policy` (`an accident on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `with` (`an illness or treatment, linked as` `directly caused by it`)) (`a burn of` 10 `percent at third degree and` 0 `percent at second degree`) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 250_000_000

§§ `Article 8.6 — emergency transport`

#ASSERT `Article 8.6 — the ambulance benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (`treated overnight in` (JUST (`an intensive care unit in` (`a facility of kind` `a hospital`) `which is an emergency room` FALSE)) `transferred` FALSE) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 1_000_000
#ASSERT `Article 8.6 — the ambulance benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (`treated overnight in` NOTHING `transferred` TRUE) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 1_000_000
#ASSERT `Article 8.6 — the ambulance benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (`treated overnight in` (JUST (`an intensive care unit in` (`a facility of kind` `a hospital`) `which is an emergency room` TRUE)) `transferred` FALSE) `nothing paid yet` `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays nothing, because` `neither an overnight stay in an intensive care unit nor a hospital transfer`
-- The 2m per contract year: 1.5m already paid leaves 0.5m; 2m leaves nothing.
#ASSERT `Article 8.6 — the ambulance benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (`treated overnight in` NOTHING `transferred` TRUE) (`already paid: permanent injury` 0 `organ` 0 `fracture` 0 `burn` 0 `ambulance this year` 1_500_000 `injury benefits for this accident` 0) `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 500_000
#ASSERT `Article 8.6 — the ambulance benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (`treated overnight in` NOTHING `transferred` TRUE) (`already paid: permanent injury` 0 `organ` 0 `fracture` 0 `burn` 0 `ambulance this year` 2_000_000 `injury benefits for this accident` 0) `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays nothing, because` `the maximum for the contract year has already been paid`

§§ `Article 8.8 and 8.9`

-- 8.8: paralysis of both legs from illness, certified at 6 months: the premiums, 30m.
#ASSERT `Article 8.8 — the disability benefit` `the policy` (`a disability of` (JUST `both legs`) `by paralysis` TRUE `capacity lost` NOTHING `from` (YMD 2027 3 10) `certified` (YMD 2027 9 10)) NOTHING `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 30_000_000
#ASSERT `Article 8.8 — the disability benefit` `the policy` (`a disability of` (JUST `both legs`) `by paralysis` TRUE `capacity lost` NOTHING `from` (YMD 2027 3 10) `certified` (YMD 2027 9 10)) (JUST `the accident`) `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays nothing, because` `the disability was caused by an Accident`
-- 8.9: 10-year term: 75% of 30m; 5-year: 50%; 15-year: 100%.
#ASSERT `Article 8.9 — the maturity benefit` `the policy` TRUE `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 22_500_000
#ASSERT `Article 8.9 — the maturity benefit` (`a policy for` 1_000_000_000 `over` 5 `years from` (YMD 2026 1 15) `on an insured born` (YMD 1990 6 1)) TRUE `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 15_000_000
#ASSERT `Article 8.9 — the maturity benefit` (`a policy for` 1_000_000_000 `over` 15 `years from` (YMD 2026 1 15) `on an insured born` (YMD 1990 6 1)) TRUE `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays` 30_000_000
#ASSERT `Article 8.9 — the maturity benefit` `the policy` FALSE `the accounts` EQUALS `Prudential pays nothing, because` `the insured was not alive at the end of the contract term`
-- A term cut short by the age-70 limit has no stated rate.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 8.9 — the maturity benefit` (`the same policy for` 1_000_000_000 `on an insured born` (YMD 1961 6 1)) TRUE `the accounts` BECAUSE "Article 8.9 states no maturity rate for a term cut short by the age-70 limit"

§§ `Article 8.10 — one Accident, several benefits, the layers together`

-- The accident is covered (1.16, no exclusion), the table gives wrist 15% + rib 10% = 250m and
-- spleen 5% = 50m, each within its cap; an ICU night adds 1m; debts of 3m come off once:
-- 250m + 50m + 1m - 3m = 298m.
#ASSERT `Article 8.10 — the total for one Accident` (LIST `Article 8.4 — the fracture benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (LIST `a fracture of` `a wrist bone` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `previously broken` NOTHING, `a fracture of` `a rib` `on` (YMD 2027 3 10) `previously broken` NOTHING) `nothing paid yet` (`the accounts before debts` `the accounts`), `Article 8.3 — the internal-organ benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (LIST `ruptured spleen`) (YMD 2027 3 10) `nothing paid yet` (`the accounts before debts` `the accounts`), `Article 8.6 — the ambulance benefit` `the policy` `the accident` (`treated overnight in` (JUST (`an intensive care unit in` (`a facility of kind` `a hospital`) `which is an emergency room` FALSE)) `transferred` FALSE) `nothing paid yet` (`the accounts before debts` `the accounts`)) (`accounts with premiums` 30_000_000 `surrender value` NOTHING `debts` (JUST 3_000_000) `medical costs` NOTHING) EQUALS 298_000_000

